{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117339","id":3386416104,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7J2Jvo","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117339","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117339.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117339.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117339","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117339/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117339/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117339/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c967fc3e9a66cefb0ba5863a3fa9b3b19058b02a","number":117339,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"2-3x Performance improvement in screen texture mipmap generation","user":{"login":"SoftLattice","id":140354190,"node_id":"U_kgDOCF2ijg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/140354190?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice","html_url":"https://github.com/SoftLattice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoftLattice/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nImproved the `copy.glsl` shader which is used in calculating mipmaps of screen textures. Performance increase has been measured at **2x-3x speedup** depending on resolution (results in table below).\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nScreen reading textures are the preferred way to perform custom post-processing. The calculation of screen texture mipmaps executes the `copy.glsl` shader multiple times per frame. As such, optimization to this shader will benefit any project that uses custom post-processing.\r\n\r\nThe current implementation doesn't take GPU subgroups into consideration. Taking advantage of subgroups, it's possible to avoid execution barriers, and eliminate cache bank collisions found in the current implementation. Making these changes can significantly improve performance (expected 2x, but observed as high as 3x).\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Changed initial texture read to linear index to encourage coalesced texture memory access\r\n- Replaced cache read/write pattern to use a shuffled index which avoids bank conflicts\r\n- Changed first Gaussian pass to compute samples fetched by the same subgroup (avoiding execution barrier)\r\n- Combined \"first pass\" glow read to initial write, eliminating a secondary cache read/write\r\n\r\n## Accuracy\r\n\r\nBenchmarks were performed executing the existing `copy.glsl` and proposed change as stand alone compute shaders. Pixel-wise absolute value differences were measured for comparison. Floating point precision differences were observed, but average per-pixel difference is measured at < 0.01%, and maximum difference (out of all pixels across all executions in batch) of < 2%.\r\n\r\nBenchmarks were performed on NVIDIA, AMD, and mobile architectures to test different subgroup sizes. Mobile by default uses a different shader, but benchmarks invoked can still be measured through compute shader execution.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\n| GPU Family | Texture Size | Mode | Old Time (us) | New Time (us)| Speedup |\r\n|-----|--------|-------|---------|---|---|\r\n| NVIDIA | 2048 | BLUR | 26.5 | 9.4 | **2.82x** |\r\n| NVIDIA | 1024 |  BLUR | 26.2 | 9.3 |**2.81x** |\r\n| NVIDIA | 512 | BLUR | 15.2 | 7.6 | **2.00x** |\r\n| NVIDIA | 1024 | GLOW | 35.0 | 12.8 | **2.73x** |\r\n| AMD | 1024 | BLUR | 13.2 | 4.3 | **3.07x** |\r\n| AMD | 1024 | GLOW | 16.0 | 5.2 | **3.07x** |\r\n\r\nFor smaller textures the overhead of kernel execution approaches shader execution time, but even at 8x8 textures a speedup of **1.63x** is observed.\r\n\r\nBenchmark project can be cloned [here](https://github.com/SoftLattice/optimized-copy-shader-benchmark).\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- The change is isolated to `servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/copy.glsl`\r\n- No AI was used to develop this code","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/